course: dictionary
lesson: 14801
title: Punjabi: a language, a person, or a description
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words can do more than one job. Punjabi can name a language, name a person, or describe something. Look at the words around it to see which job it does. «Priya speaks Punjabi at home.» Here Punjabi names a language, so it is a noun.
explain: «We ate Punjabi food at the party.» Here Punjabi is an adjective. It tells you what kind of food it was. Ask yourself: is this word naming something, or describing something?
explain: Capital letters matter. Punjabi always starts with a capital P. «Mr Singh is Punjabi.» Here it means a person from the Punjab region. The words around the word, and what they are about, tell you which meaning fits.
fact: The Punjab is a region of India and Pakistan.
fact: Punjabi is a language spoken in the Punjab, and by many people in the UK, Canada and elsewhere.
fact: «Punjabi» can be a noun for a language, a noun for a person, or an adjective meaning connected with the Punjab.
fact: «Punjabi food», such as samosas and naan, and bhangra music are popular in many places.
fact: Many Sikhs are Punjabi.
exercise: «Amrit speaks Punjabi at home.» In this sentence, what does Punjabi name? | *A language | A dance | A kind of music | A food
exercise: «We ate Punjabi food at the party: samosas and naan.» What kind of word is Punjabi here? | A noun naming a person | A verb for doing something | *An adjective, describing the food | A name for a town
exercise: Which of these is a Punjabi food? | Sushi | *Naan | Pizza | Tacos
test: «The Punjabi music made everyone dance.» What does Punjabi mean here? | A town in England | *Connected with the Punjab, describing the music | A person | A language
test: «Mrs Kaur is Punjabi, and she comes from the Punjab region.» What does Punjabi mean in this sentence? | A kind of food | A school subject | A type of weather | *A person from the Punjab region
exam: «He has learnt to read Punjabi at weekend school.» What does Punjabi name here? | A dance | *A language | A festival | A place
